{
  "assembly_notes": "Round dining table with a lazy-susan turntable. One rigid tabletop root carries the round slab, its edge band, the circular apron, the radial underframe and every support mount. A single turntable_tray is a REVOLUTE (+z) child of the tabletop on a central bearing; it is continuous, so lower=-pi and upper=+pi. tray_build changes the tray plan itself (woven lattice, flush recessed pocket, raised guard rim, two-tier post or wedge sectors) and bearing_build independently changes the mechanism it turns on (flat race and plate, wide annular ring with a spoked hub, caged rollers on a tray-side track, or a pocketed detent ring indexed by a tray-mounted spring pin). Every tray plan combines with every bearing because the host derives one mount height for all of them: woven_lattice, flush_recessed (host pocket plus bearing lip), indexed_detent (host detent ring, tray spring pin), raised_guard_rim, ring_bearing (host annular race instead of a central pedestal), roller_bearing (host roller retainer), two_tier (host lower shelf) and segmented_wedge. base_build is one structural family of table bases: folding_legs hinges support_count square-tube legs off the underframe on fork-and-pin brackets, while pedestal_column and tripod_pedestal stand on a central column whose hub carries support_count feet. Every base therefore has exactly support_count members and grows with it. table_diameter_m, tray_diameter_ratio and table_height_m are the independent parameters; palette, weave density and fastener counts are non-core.",
